text:
JWT `exp` in **seconds**. `Date.now()` in **milliseconds**.

**Bug:**
```js
if (Date.now() > payload.exp) // wrong — always false, exp looks huge
```

**Fix:**
```js
if (Date.now() / 1000 > payload.exp) // convert ms → s
// or
if (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp)
```

**Full middleware:**
```js
function authMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'No token' });

  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    // jwt.verify() checks expiry automatically — see note below
    req.user = payload;
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid or expired token' });
  }
}
```

**Better:** `jwt.verify()` from `jsonwebtoken` checks `exp` automatically. Manual check redundant + error-prone. Drop manual check, let library handle it. Throws `TokenExpiredError` on expiry — catch covers it.

Only manual-check if using raw `jwt.decode()` (no verification). Don't do that.
